Done. Implemented the **Robot Name** exercise.

**What I implemented** (`robot_name.py`):
- `Robot.__init__` generates a random name in the format `AA123` (two uppercase letters + three digits) on first instantiation.
- `Robot.reset()` wipes the name and generates a new random one on the next access.
- Names are random via `random.choice` over letter/digit pools (no predictable sequence), and a class-level `_used_names` set guarantees every existing robot has a unique name.

